    "findings": [
      "The package is a policy and validation surface; it performs no network I/O, TLS handshake, DNS resolution or backend execution. The @galerina/tower-citizen workspace dependency is an explicit boundary and must remain provenance-visible.",
      "Seven loaded Fungi assets cover admission feedback, B8 admission, cert gates, CORS, defensive controls, egress and inbound decisions; their RD-0361 execution tests are bounded comparisons and do not establish replacement or authority.",
      "Policy/report helpers use unfrozen shared TLS/privacy defaults and caller-provided collections. Backend selection trusts supplied capabilities, first duplicate wins, and requireSafeFallback:false can report satisfied for an unavailable or unsafe fallback.",
      "Network policy validation is deny-by-default and TLS-first, but minimum TLS, self-signed policy and privacy flags are not all runtime-enforced by the validator; exact diagnostic order, trim, includes, Set and numeric port semantics are observable.",
      "Host classification canonicalizes decimal, hex, octal and mapped IPv6 forms, treats hostnames as requiring DNS re-check, and guardResolvedAddresses consumes supplied addresses rather than resolving or pinning connections. Allow-list exceptions and URL credentials are security boundaries.",
      "Production egress policy distinguishes metadata, non-public, plaintext and credential relaxations; policy diagnostics do not enforce a dial, and validateWebhookTarget intentionally ignores caller relaxations.",
      "Inbound admission accepts port 0 unlike declarative validation, missing protocol can match any protocol, empty rule ports match all ports, and explicit deny wins. RateLimiter mutates a persistent Map and trusts supplied time; pruning, rule changes and window boundaries need proof.",
      "CORS uses exact origin matching, null denial, wildcard/credential incompatibility and case-insensitive preflight checks; header and method array mutation/order affect outputs.",
      "CertGate folds K3 factors with revocation freshness and fail-closed unknown handling; supplied revocation outcomes, timestamps and callbacks are not independently verified. Callback order and thrown-error propagation are observable.",
      "Telemetry feedback is degrade-only; empty telemetry is the identity, and revocation cadence degrades to chunk-boundary checks with no never mode.",
      "Backend and host decisions remain metadata/decision outputs. No helper grants production authority, switches consumers, retires TypeScript or enforces a seal.",
      "The external tower-citizen import path and built artifact identity need separate source and module-boundary proof before any translation wave."
    ]
  },
